## ============================================================================
## General
## ============================================================================
##
## The engine authenticates its API here as it does on Kubernetes. The break-glass
## login is DFE_AUTH_LOCAL_ADMIN_NAME plus DFE_AUTH_LOCAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD, which
## `make init` generates into .env and the engine seeds on its FIRST start. An
## OIDC issuer in front fronts the proxy origin only, never this API's machine
## paths, and dfe-docker never assumes one exists. See docs/operating.md.
#
# DFE_AUTH_LOCAL_ADMIN_NAME=admin
# DFE_API_PORT=8003

## ============================================================================
## External OIDC login -- the engine as the relying party
## ============================================================================
##
## Not the DFE_OIDC_* keys in .env. Those belong to the oauth2-proxy in front of
## the infra UIs and are its own client. These are the credentials the ENGINE
## uses to run a login at /api/v1/auth/oidc/<provider>/login, and the two sets
## must not be pointed at one another.
##
## A provider is a YAML file the engine reads from
## $DFE_CONFIG_DIR/auth/oidc-providers/<provider>.yaml. That file names the
## variables its credentials live in (client_id_env, client_secret_env) and
## never carries the secret itself, so the names below are a convention, not a
## contract -- if your provider file names something else, set that instead.
##
## Register the callback with the IdP as
##   <engine base as the browser reaches it>/api/v1/auth/oidc/<provider>/callback
## Through dfe-proxy the base is the UI origin; straight at the API it is
## DFE_ENGINE_PORT. Those are separate origins to an IdP, so register both.
#
## A provider file of type `generic` -- dex and anything standards-only
# DFE_OIDC_DEX_CLIENT_ID=
# DFE_OIDC_DEX_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
## Microsoft Entra ID
# DFE_OIDC_ENTRA_CLIENT_ID=
# DFE_OIDC_ENTRA_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
## Okta
# DFE_OIDC_OKTA_CLIENT_ID=
# DFE_OIDC_OKTA_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
## Google Workspace. Google puts no groups in any token, so the engine resolves
## them through the Admin SDK Directory API instead, with the service account
## JSON in the variable the provider file's groups.service_account_json_env
## names. Without it a Google login succeeds and every user lands with no roles.
# DFE_OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# DFE_OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# DFE_GOOGLE_SA_JSON=
#
## An IdP whose certificate comes from a private CA: mount a bundle into the
## engine container and point this at it, or OIDC discovery fails verifying the
## chain. It REPLACES the default trust store rather than adding to it, so the
## file has to be a full bundle -- the public roots with your CA appended.
# SSL_CERT_FILE=/etc/ssl/certs/idp-bundle.crt

## ===========================================================================
## ClickHouse Configuration
## ===========================================================================
#
# DFE_CLICKHOUSE_BOOTSTRAP_TABLES=true
# DFE_CLICKHOUSE_DATA_DATABASE=dfe
# DFE_CLICKHOUSE_LANDING_TABLE=default
#
# DFE_CLICKHOUSE_CONNECTIONS_MIN=10
# DFE_CLICKHOUSE_CONNECTIONS_MAX=300

## ===========================================================================
## Kafka Configuration
## ===========================================================================
#
# DFE_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9092
# DFE_KAFKA_SECURITY_PROTOCOL=SASL_PLAINTEXT
# DFE_KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM=SCRAM-SHA-256
# DFE_KAFKA_SASL_USERNAME=<kafka-user>
# DFE_KAFKA_SASL_PASSWORD=<kafka-password>
#
## With TLS - Port 9093 (uncomment to use)
# DFE_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=your-kafka-host.example.com:9093
# DFE_KAFKA_SECURITY_PROTOCOL=SASL_SSL
#
## Without auth (uncomment for plain local dev)
# DFE_KAFKA_SECURITY_PROTOCOL=PLAINTEXT

## ============================================================================
## Helm Compiler Configuration
## ============================================================================
#
# DFE_HELM_OUTPUT_DIR=
# DFE_HELM_ENVIRONMENT_FILE=

## ============================================================================
## Hunt Scheduler Settings
## ============================================================================
#
# DFE_HUNT_LOG_PATH=hunt_log_path

## ============================================================================
## Storage Configuration (for on-prem/Rancher deployments)
## ============================================================================
#
# DFE_STORAGE_TYPE=auto
# DFE_STORAGE_PATH=./artifacts
# DFE_S3_BUCKET=
# DFE_S3_REGION=

## ============================================================================
## Integration Testing (point a local engine at an external cluster)
## ============================================================================
## Overrides that let a local dfe-engine talk to a REMOTE Kubernetes cluster,
## Argo CD, OTel collector, ClickHouse or Kafka - e.g. running the k8s
## integration/e2e suite against a shared environment. Fill in YOUR target's
## hosts. These deliberately carry no real hostnames: on the HyperI devex fleet
## hyperi-infra injects the concrete values from OpenBao at test time, so the
## estate topology stays out of this committed template.
#
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Kubernetes
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# KUBECONFIG=~/.kube/config
# KUBECONTEXT=your-context
#
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Argo CD
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARGOCD_SERVER=argocd.your-cluster.example.com
# ARGOCD_AUTH_TOKEN=
#
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## OTel Collector
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector.your-cluster.example.com:4317
#
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## ClickHouse (override the in-stack default)
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DFE_CLICKHOUSE_HOST=clickhouse.your-cluster.example.com
#
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Kafka (override the in-stack default)
## ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DFE_KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=kafka.your-cluster.example.com:9092

# =============================================================================
# Elastic Schema Service Configuration
# =============================================================================
# DFE_ELASTIC_CONVERTER_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=5242880 # 5 * 1024 * 1024 - 5MB
# DFE_ELASTIC_CONVERTER_READ_CHUNK_SIZE=65536 # 64 * 1024 - 64KB
# DFE_ELASTIC_CONVERTER_CONTENT_LENGTH_SLACK_BYTES=262144 # 256 * 1024 - 256KB
